{"year":"1930","content":[{"type":"text","content_text":"In 1930 the Academy held two ceremonies. The 2nd, on April 3, at the Cocoanut Grove of the Ambassador Hotel in Los Angeles, honored films released between August 1928 and July 1929; the 3rd, on November 5, honored those released between August 1929 and July 1930. That is why, on this page, each category shows its edition in the name: \"(April)\" for the 2nd ceremony and \"(November)\" for the 3rd."},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Best Picture (April)","nominee_list":[{"type":"movie","id":65203,"name":"Melodia da Broadway","image_path":"/dGUwu9Z38jI9YkHf0StGkhkmwhY.jpg","director":"Harry Beaumont","winner":true,"backdrop_path":"/tEAEturRMtH4uY3wq2xvlINgiVj.jpg"},{"type":"movie","id":13847,"name":"Alibi","image_path":"/2C3ZDxVrOVafzNoOVrxsNQDiHey.jpg","director":"Roland West","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":31678,"name":"The Hollywood Revue of 1929","image_path":"/pe8dZ8LpRnfivsQ7nxLhH5AWxoW.jpg","director":"Charles Reisner","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":83989,"name":"In Old Arizona","image_path":"/x1XSQeLUdoi72P5UOXqAyL46B9a.jpg","director":"Irving Cummings, Raoul Walsh","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":83990,"name":"The Patriot","image_path":"/2eDSqz95WrPKLMPllZlEe2iKpYE.jpg","director":"Ernst Lubitsch","winner":false}]},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Best Picture (November)","nominee_list":[{"type":"movie","id":143,"name":"Sem Novidade no Front","image_path":"/7kJgNZaRAOYM3HJIP5eTZ8PWVv4.jpg","director":"Lewis Milestone","winner":true,"backdrop_path":"/yeQGyB8MjpX8KR7rUrP0E3gaviC.jpg"},{"type":"movie","id":47250,"name":"The Big House","image_path":"/qVf7Dpgx0sdDkZEn4CwTYethoMp.jpg","director":"George W. Hill","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":84274,"name":"Disraeli","image_path":"/uVTmxQJp0sqBujbieSTrB2ui9al.jpg","director":"Alfred E. Green","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":80708,"name":"The Divorcee","image_path":"/zzu6IW9ilkUt6L4DL9SoNnwtAfy.jpg","director":"Robert Z. Leonard","